From d2443d22120020d8c6ad9793e41c38b4d5d762b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 21:53:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] USB audio from mastertune: the Deluge's output as a USB audio
 input on the computer, the song's name for a recorder

Ports mastertune 1.2.1's USB audio (its patches 0008, 0055 and 0112) onto v1.3. io/usb/usb_audio*, usb_song_info* and
the Renesas driver's changes are mastertune's (they applied unchanged); the glue is fitted to v1.3: the community
features are read before USB starts (v1.3's readSettingsFromFile() without arguments), the frames pushed are v1.3's
outputBufferForResampling, the setting is the last of v1.3's community features, the song info goes out on v1.3's
USB MIDI cable 3, its task and the gaps' task are registered with RESOURCE_NONE.

- Settings > Community features > USB audio (off by default, read at boot): the Deluge enumerates as a USB Audio Class
  1.0 device next to its MIDI interface, stereo, 24 bits, 44.1 kHz; the computer records exactly what goes to the
  outputs. Empty packets the computer got show "USB audio gap", at most every 10 s. Nothing during an offline stem
  export.
- The setting is saved at once when it changes ("Restart to apply"), so a restart from the menu keeps it; that save
  keeps the startup song as it was (as the CPU monitor's save), so a song loaded but not saved doesn't become the one
  "Last saved" opens.
- While the computer has the stream open, the song's name and the firmware go to USB MIDI port 3 as SysEx 0x12 (JSON,
  packed 7 bits in 8) for DelugeRec.
